A||||18||Eric Marsh||Tach Filter and MSD Ignition||||5
Z||000000||Eric Marsh||10-22-1999||02:50 PM||||I'm trying to get my stock tack to work with an MSD 6-AL ignition system. I've attached the white wire in the wiring harness that comes out of the firewall to the tach output of the MSD unit but I'm not getting any action. Has anyone been through this before?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||10-22-1999||03:26 PM||||I have a 6al on my 4cyl se and I used the GM style blaster coil and the adapter harnes to make it all work without cutting into the factory wiring. The tach works fine without wiring it to the MSD box. I dont know how you wired yours, but you should not have had to change the tach wiring to make it work.||||reg||14
Z||000002||Eric Marsh||10-22-1999||03:29 PM||||I've got MSD everything, (coil, distributer, plug wires, etc.) so I don't know if your solution will work. I've considered trying to attach the tach wire to the coil and see what that does.<P>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-22-1999||07:16 PM||||Attach the tach wire to the same wire as the distributor module's coil output. It's less noisy. your also less likely to fry the tach filter.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||10-23-1999||05:53 PM||||Did you get it working?||||reg||5
Z||000005||pollock||10-26-1999||10:38 AM||||Some tachs, especially factory ones, require an additional adapter from MSD.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Eric Marsh||10-26-1999||12:13 PM||||Nope, I have not yet got it working. GM products don't require adaptors but that filter is supposed to be removed. I might try jumping around the tack lead and see if that makes a difference.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cooter||10-26-1999||08:18 PM||||I just disected the MSD adapter harness that I used on my car to get the wiring order for you:<BR>   The large red wire from the car and the red wire from the distributer are tied together.<BR>   The white wire from the car and the distributer are tied together.<BR>   The RED wire from the MSD is tied to the TWO red wires from the factory ignition.<BR>   The WHITE wire from the MSD is tied to the TWO white wires from the factory ignition.<BR>   The ORANGE and BROWN msd wires are connected to the coil. <BR>   If your's is not wired like this, with the tach filter in place, it will not work. The tach signal from the distributer is used to trigger the msd AND the tach off the same lead. The factory tach will not work off the MSD tach plug without the  optional msd tach adapter.||||reg||14
Z||000008||Greg Piet||10-27-1999||04:52 AM||||Thinking of going to MSD ignition.   Where is the best price????    I found a module for 174.00 US, but then they have extra charges for wiring harnesses etc....   any reccomendation?<P><BR>Also...  Stroker if your out there, will the MSD 6AL be peachy with your turbo kit?||||reg||1
Z||000009||mwbackus||10-27-1999||07:35 AM||||Greg:<BR>With the exception of the 88's, a rev limiter is already present on the factory ECM chip.  Therefore, you may want to opt for the 6A rather than the 6AL.  Summit Racing Equipment has some good pricing on MSD products:<P>1 - MSD-6200    MSD 6A Ignition Control			$130.95<P>1 - MSD-8876    Harness for GM Dual Connector		$ 27.95<P>Jegs also has comparable pricing on the above.<P>Mike||||reg||1
Z||000010||Cooter||10-27-1999||02:32 PM||||The MSD adapter harness is a good thing to have! It makes installation a simple plug in procedure and if the unit ever fails, you can quickly unplug it and go back to the original system.||||reg||1
Z||000011||BOILERMAKER||10-28-1999||09:28 AM||||The MSD-6A can go onto a stock 2.8 engine without any other mods, right?  I am thinking of buying this and installing it on my 2.8 so that I know it works when it finally goes to the rebuilt 3.1.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cooter||10-28-1999||02:25 PM||||I have a 6al on my 2.5 Duckmobile. It works great on the stock system- but I do have the GM style blaster coil with it. I left the old coil in place in case the MSD fails, I can switch back by swapping the plug back to it.||||reg||14
Z||000013||BOILERMAKER||11-05-1999||07:50 AM||||If I get this GM Blaster coil with the rest of the MSD ignition (MSD-6A) will the coil sit in the same spot that the original does without modification?  If not, then how was yours installed?  I am planning on putting the 6A in the trunk like I have seen many people do, but haven't seen where they put the coil.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Greg Piet||11-05-1999||08:16 AM||||Just to note:<BR>If anyone out there is planning on going to a  turbo at a later date(like me), The MSD-6BTC might be a better option.  It costs more, but it will automatically retard the timing if boost changes.  <P>From the pictures of the GM blaster, it appears to look exactly like the stock coil, so I assume it can be mounted in place of the stock coil.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Cooter||11-05-1999||08:42 AM||||I mounted the blaster coil on the rear firewall beside the cruise actuator. I left the stock coil in place so if anything happened to the blaster or MSD I could go back to the stock ignition. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||BOILERMAKER||11-05-1999||10:11 AM||||I was going to use the MSD-6A along with the MSD-8762.<P>Is this MSD-6BTC both of these items tied up in one?  No one has mentioned it.  That's why I was wondering.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Greg Piet||11-05-1999||11:18 AM||||Im not sure what the 8762 is (GM blaster coil?)<BR>I know the BTC picture looks like the 6A, but it said it has a way to set the amount of retard for each PSI of boost.  The GM blaster coil should work with any of the 6 series, bu ti think you need the wiring harness||||reg||1
Z||000018||mwbackus||11-05-1999||02:43 PM||||The 8762 is the MSD Boost Timing Master, it is used in conjunction with an MSD 6 ignition.  The 6 BTM combines the 6A and the Boost Timing Master into one box.  There is no cost advantage in the purchase of the 6 BTM over the two separate components (6A and 8762).  It makes much more sense to purchase the separate components.  Much easier to isolate a failure and replace one component rather than the whole thing.  Of course, if the magical cheapo turbo system does not become a reality, than you just saved yourself a chunk of money. ;-)<BR>||||reg||1
